{title: Looking Through The Eyes of Faith}
{artist: Larry Holder, Elton Smith and Steve Israel}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 87}

Introduction
[Bb] [F] [Gm] [Dm] [Eb] [F] [Eb] [F] [Eb] [Bb] [F]

Verse 1
Looking [Bb]through the [Cm]eyes of [Dm]faith, [Eb]
We [Bb]see as our [F]Father [Gm]sees. [Eb]
It will [Bb]make our [Cm]hearts cry [Dm]out with [Eb]joy,
It will [C7]bring us to our [F]knees.
For [Bb]there up[Cm]on the [Dm]throne [Eb]
Our [Bb]Savior [F]reigns on [Gm]high. [Eb]
The [Bb]stars quake [Cm]in the [Dm]heavens, [Eb]
And [C7]all creation [F]cries:

Chorus
He is [Bb]Holy He is [F]Lord!
[Dm]Worthy is the Lamb of [Gm]God.
He's the [Bb]One Eternal [F]Word,
Come, [Gm]gather [Dm]'round the [Eb]throne of [F]grace.
He is [Bb]Holy He is [F]Lord!
Hear the [Dm]angels join our [Gm]song.
All [Bb]glory, [Cm]honor, [Dm]majes[Eb]ty [Dm] [Cm] [Bb]
Un[C7]to the [F]Lord be[Bb]long!

Short solo
[F] [Gm] [Dm] [Eb] [F]

Verse 2
Looking [Bb]through the [Cm]eyes of [Dm]faith, [Eb]
We [Bb]share our [F]Father's [Gm]heart. [Eb]
We can [Bb]see He's [Cm]hbrought to[Dm]gether [Eb]now
What [C7]once was torn a[F]part.
And we [Bb]need not [Cm]fear to[Dm]morrow: [Eb]
For the [Bb]battle [F]has been [Gm]won. [Eb]
We [Bb]now pro[Cm]claim the [Dm]holy Name [Eb]
Of Mes[C7]siah, God's own [F]Son!

